1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,020
So far every sum we've done has used one rod.

2
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:07,260
Today we're using two and it's easier than it sounds.

3
00:00:07,980 --> 00:00:10,620
Remember each rod has its own place.

4
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:13,740
The rod on the right is the ones rod.

5
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:17,040
The rod next to it is the tens rod.

6
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:20,920
Together they can show every number up to ninety-nine.

7
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:23,640
Here's the whole trick for today.

8
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:27,160
We never work on two rods at the same time.

9
00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:28,820
We do one rod.

10
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:31,460
Then the other rod.

11
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:35,060
Each rod is just a small sum on its own.

12
00:00:36,220 --> 00:00:38,320
Let's try twenty-one plus three.

13
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:40,600
First make twenty-one.

14
00:00:41,660 --> 00:00:44,240
Push two lower beads up on the tens rod.

15
00:00:44,940 --> 00:00:47,620
Push one lower bead up on the ones rod.

16
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:50,420
The abacus is showing twenty-one.

17
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:52,660
Now we add three.

18
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:57,320
Three is a ones number so only the ones rod moves.

19
00:00:58,020 --> 00:01:00,980
Push three more lower beads up on the ones rod.

20
00:01:01,580 --> 00:01:03,620
The tens rod doesn't move at all.

21
00:01:04,220 --> 00:01:05,640
It's still showing twenty.

22
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:08,460
And the ones rod is showing four.

23
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:11,960
So twenty-one plus three is twenty-four.

24
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:14,820
Now let's move both rods.

25
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:18,140
Let's try fourteen plus twenty-five.

26
00:01:19,220 --> 00:01:20,540
First make fourteen.

27
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:23,900
Push one lower bead up on the tens rod.

28
00:01:24,540 --> 00:01:27,320
Push four lower beads up on the ones rod.

29
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:29,480
Now we add twenty-five.

30
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:32,160
Twenty-five is twenty.

31
00:01:32,860 --> 00:01:33,680
And five.

32
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:36,020
Let's start with the tens rod.

33
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:38,980
Twenty means two more tens.

34
00:01:39,440 --> 00:01:42,260
Push two more lower beads up on the tens rod.

35
00:01:42,820 --> 00:01:45,660
The tens rod is now showing three tens.

36
00:01:46,260 --> 00:01:47,280
Now the ones rod.

37
00:01:48,220 --> 00:01:49,880
Five lives on the upper bead.

38
00:01:50,380 --> 00:01:51,940
So push the upper bead down.

39
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:54,400
The ones rod is showing nine.

40
00:01:55,100 --> 00:01:57,260
Three tens and nine ones.

41
00:01:57,840 --> 00:02:00,760
So fourteen plus twenty-five is thirty-nine.

42
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:03,500
Did you see what we did?

43
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:06,900
Two little sums one after the other.

44
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:09,800
That's all a big sum ever is.

45
00:02:10,980 --> 00:02:12,920
Taking away works the same way.

46
00:02:13,660 --> 00:02:16,260
Let's try thirty-nine take away fifteen.

47
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:19,840
Our abacus is already showing thirty-nine.

48
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:23,480
Fifteen is ten and five.

49
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:25,760
Start with the tens rod again.

50
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:28,680
Ten means one ten goes away.

51
00:02:29,420 --> 00:02:32,100
Push one lower bead down on the tens rod.

52
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:35,540
The tens rod is now showing two tens.

53
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:37,300
Now the ones rod.

54
00:02:37,980 --> 00:02:39,740
We need to take away five.

55
00:02:40,380 --> 00:02:43,180
Five is the upper bead so push it back up.

56
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:46,000
The four lower beads stay where they are.

57
00:02:46,330 --> 00:02:48,800
Two tens and four ones.

58
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:52,640
So thirty-nine take away fifteen is twenty-four.

59
00:02:54,030 --> 00:02:55,280
Now it's your turn.

60
00:02:56,040 --> 00:02:58,200
Make twenty-three on your own abacus.

61
00:02:58,520 --> 00:02:59,700
Then add eleven.

62
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:03,020
Remember one rod at a time.

63
00:03:03,940 --> 00:03:05,520
What number is showing now?

64
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:11,300
Twenty-three plus eleven is thirty-four.

65
00:03:12,060 --> 00:03:12,660
Great job.

66
00:03:13,740 --> 00:03:17,380
Try a few more two rod sums on your own abacus.

67
00:03:17,860 --> 00:03:22,080
If you enjoyed this video, please like and subscribe for more.

68
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:26,800
Search for abacus kids on the Apple App Store or Google Play.

69
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:28,580
Download it free.

70
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:31,160
Next time something different.

71
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:37,240
We'll try a sum the beads can't do and learn the clever trick that fixes it.
